Task 2: Create Network Policies to Control VM Communication
Subtask 2.1: Create Default Deny Network Policy
Network Policies in OpenShift control traffic flow between pods and VMs at the IP address or port level.

Create a default deny-all network policy:
Create a file named default-deny-policy.yaml:

apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: default-deny-all
  namespace: vm-networking-lab
spec:
  podSelector: {}
  policyTypes:
  - Ingress
  - Egress
Apply the default deny policy:
oc apply -f default-deny-policy.yaml
Subtask 2.2: Create Selective Allow Policies
Create a policy to allow VM-to-VM communication:
Create a file named allow-vm-to-vm.yaml:

apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: allow-vm-to-vm
  namespace: vm-networking-lab
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      kubevirt.io/vm: vm1-static
  policyTypes:
  - Ingress
  - Egress
  ingress:
  - from:
    - podSelector:
        matchLabels:
          kubevirt.io/vm: vm2-static
    ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 22
    - protocol: ICMP
  egress:
  - to:
    - podSelector:
        matchLabels:
          kubevirt.io/vm: vm2-static
    ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 22
    - protocol: ICMP
  - to: {}
    ports:
    - protocol: UDP
      port: 53
Create a reciprocal policy for VM2:
Create a file named allow-vm2-to-vm1.yaml:

apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: allow-vm2-to-vm1
  namespace: vm-networking-lab
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      kubevirt.io/vm: vm2-static
  policyTypes:
  - Ingress
  - Egress
  ingress:
  - from:
    - podSelector:
        matchLabels:
          kubevirt.io/vm: vm1-static
    ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 22
    - protocol: ICMP
  egress:
  - to:
    - podSelector:
        matchLabels:
          kubevirt.io/vm: vm1-static
    ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 22
    - protocol: ICMP
  - to: {}
    ports:
    - protocol: UDP
      port: 53
Apply the network policies:
oc apply -f allow-vm-to-vm.yaml
oc apply -f allow-vm2-to-vm1.yaml
Subtask 2.3: Create External Access Policy
Create a policy allowing external internet access:
Create a file named allow-external-access.yaml:

apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: allow-external-access
  namespace: vm-networking-lab
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      kubevirt.io/vm: vm1-static
  policyTypes:
  - Egress
  egress:
  - to: []
    ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 80
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 443
    - protocol: UDP
      port: 53
Apply the external access policy:
oc apply -f allow-external-access.yaml
Verify all network policies are created:
oc get networkpolicies -n vm-networking-lab
