Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: VMs Not Getting Static IPs
Symptoms: VMs start but don't have the expected static IP addresses.

Solution:

# Check network attachment definition
oc get network-attachment-definitions -n vm-networking-lab

# Verify VM network configuration
oc describe vmi vm1-static -n vm-networking-lab

# Check cloud-init logs inside VM
sudo journalctl -u cloud-init
Issue 2: Network Policies Not Working
Symptoms: Traffic is allowed when it should be blocked, or blocked when it should be allowed.

Solution:

# Verify network policies are applied
oc get networkpolicies -n vm-networking-lab

# Check pod labels match policy selectors
oc get pods -n vm-networking-lab --show-labels

# Test with temporary policy removal
oc delete networkpolicy default-deny-all -n vm-networking-lab
Issue 3: VM Console Connection Issues
Symptoms: Cannot connect to VM console using virtctl.

Solution:

# Check VM status
oc get vms -n vm-networking-lab
oc get vmis -n vm-networking-lab

# Verify virtctl is properly configured
virtctl version

# Try alternative connection method
oc get pods -n vm-networking-lab
oc exec -it <virt-launcher-pod> -- /bin/bash
Verification and Testing Scripts
Create a comprehensive test script named network-test.sh:

#!/bin/bash

echo "=== VM Networking Lab Verification ==="

# Test 1: Check VMs are running
